{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrP5ByFkg7oZqEGAytjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see the source of the function, so this diagnosis comes from the call graph and the report. The most likely cause is that `AuthService.resetPassword` updates the password but never deletes the user's existing sessions.\n\nThe graph shows `.resetPassword()` (`auth.service.ts` L367) calling only `.getForgotSecret()`, `.findById()` and `.update()` (L415). It makes no call to the session service. Refresh tokens are validated against session records. If those survive a reset, an already signed-in phone can keep renewing its login.\n\n<function_calls>\n<invoke name=\"StructuredOutput\">\n<parameter name=\"candidates\">[{\"file\":\"src/auth/auth.service.ts\",\"symbol\":\"AuthService.resetPassword\",\"start_line\":367,\"end_line\":420,\"explanation\":\"After verifying the reset hash, the method only updates the user's password (usersService.update at ~L415). It does not invalidate the user's existing sessions (no sessionService.deleteByUserId call). Existing refresh tokens still point to valid sessions, so devices that were already signed in can keep refreshing after a password reset.\"},{\"file\":\"src/auth/auth.service.ts\",\"symbol\":\"AuthService.refreshToken\",\"start_line\":519,\"end_line\":560,\"explanation\":\"Refresh only looks up the user and issues new tokens (findById, getTokensData). Because resetPassword leaves old sessions in place, nothing here rejects a refresh made with a token issued before the reset.\"}]</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"fix\">{\"file\":\"src/auth/auth.service.ts\",\"description\":\"In AuthService.resetPassword, delete all of the user's sessions when the password is changed. Call `await this.sessionService.deleteByUserId({ userId: user.id })` before or after `usersService.update(user.id, { password })`. Inject SessionService into AuthService if it isn't already, and add a `deleteByUserId` method to it if it doesn't exist.\"}</parameter>\n</invoke>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":66289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1982a38-2171-4215-86cc-74c9e70a20b2","uuid":"52a41c32-a1a2-420d-a503-970a3fdb2436","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:08:33.512Z","request_id":"req_011CgrP5BnM3YjmCyVraxca4"}
